From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:31:13 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] platform-ngp

NeoGeo Pocket and Pocket Color get one shelf, Games/NGP, on Beetle NeoPop
(mednafen_ngp) alone. Platform::Ngp is appended to SHELVES and
Core::MednafenNgp to EVERY; upstream's ALL lists stay as they are. Carts
are .ngp, .ngc and .ngpc (.npc is in no No-Intro dat) and list under
their file stem. slot_store::ngp reads the header: the SNK signature, the
colour byte at 0x23 (0x10 Color, anything else mono) and the 12-byte
title; a short or unsigned file still lists, as mono.

Every policy method answers NGP explicitly: slot keeps L1 and R1, X and
Y stay turbo, Select+X flips the picture, no core picker, no crop or
overscan, rewind on, and the 160x152 picture sits in the GBA-sized
240x160 canvas. Its shader is stored in Config/ngp_shader.txt and offers
the Game Gear list (Off, LCD3x, then the retro list). Saves/NGP,
States/NGP and Labels/NGP are made at boot. The shelf shows a
placeholder GBA shape until the NGP carts land.

The shelf shape follows nelynes/slotPlus a8eae4c (GPL-3.0), reimplemented.
The generated test cart moves to ngp_common for every NGP test.
